                        "entry_id": "8f77e515-38ce-30d3-945a-0cba743a3da4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "附記，補說；針對書籍（特別是經典著作）特定部分文本的較詳盡論述（通常在獨立的章節中）"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2c270e5-1f04-3821-a01e-adca5f911d0a",
                        "entry_id": "8f77e515-38ce-30d3-945a-0cba743a3da4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "敘事時的離題（尤指為了討論特定議題）"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14da99fd-f8e1-465c-b78c-c63ffe585b23",
                                "sense_id": "b2c270e5-1f04-3821-a01e-adca5f911d0a",
                                "text": "Here is what us scholars call an excursus. If you are an honest man the following page or two can be of no possible interest to you.",
                                "translation": "這就是我們這些學者所說的「偏題論述」。如果你是個老實人，接下來的一兩頁可能對你毫無吸引力。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2bf2153-89dd-40b2-be58-c7e75fff08db",
                                "sense_id": "b2c270e5-1f04-3821-a01e-adca5f911d0a",
                                "text": "In his excursus on the Jewish people at the opening of the fifth book of his Histories [...], Tacitus was at a loss to uncover any deep cause for the war that broke out in 66.",
                                "translation": "塔西佗在其《歷史》第五卷開篇關於猶太人的偏題論述中 …，對於公元66年爆發的戰爭，他無法找出任何深層原因。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d3c5da49-8168-4d4c-9d8d-4242d9ea37c1",
                                "sense_id": "b2c270e5-1f04-3821-a01e-adca5f911d0a",
                                "text": "Part III (Chapters 12 to 16) includes an excursus which leads us to the use of Esperanto outside the community of its speakers.",
                                "translation": "第三部分（第12至16章）包含了一個偏題論述，引領我們探討世界語在其使用者社群之外的使用情況。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65d05544-5eea-4ae7-993c-425a31d92dd7",
                                "sense_id": "b2c270e5-1f04-3821-a01e-adca5f911d0a",
                                "text": "The authors devote a fascinating excursus to the Western imagination’s preoccupation with serpents—from Eden to esoterica—and how this primed the ground for Kuṇḍalinī’s reception.",
                                "translation": "作者用一段引人入勝的偏題論述探討了西方想像中對蛇的痴迷——從伊甸園到秘傳教理——以及這如何為昆達里尼的接受奠定了基礎。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
